course: dictionary
lesson: 8884
title: One word, many meanings: shower
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Shower is a good example. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Keep showers short, around five minutes, to save water and energy.» Short and save water tell you this is about the bathroom kind of shower.
explain: «Meteor showers happen when the Earth passes through trails of dust left by comets, such as the Perseids every August.» Here, dust, comets and Earth tell you a shower is a lot of small things falling together, not water at all.
explain: Shower can also be a verb, a doing word. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A shower is a device that sprays water on you from above to wash your body.
fact: A shower can also be a short period of rain or snow, as in «April showers».
fact: A meteor shower is many shooting stars, or small pieces of dust burning up, falling together.
fact: «Shower and use the toilet before you swim»: sweat and wee can mix with chlorine in the pool, so washing first helps.
fact: Keep showers short, around five minutes, to save water and energy.
exercise: «Keep showers short, around five minutes, to save water.» In this sentence, what does shower mean? | A short period of rain | To give someone a lot of something | A party where people bring presents | *A device that sprays water on you
exercise: «The Perseids are a meteor shower seen every August.» What is a meteor shower? | A party for a new baby | A type of soap | A short bath before bed | *Many shooting stars falling together
exercise: Grandad says, «Let's shower them with gifts.» What does shower mean here? | To dry off with a towel | To wash under a shower | *To give someone a lot of something | To fall in short bursts from clouds
test:  Ella says, «Use soap when you shower after sport.» What does shower mean here? | A party where people bring presents | *To wash under a shower | To give someone a lot of something | A shower of sparks from a fire
test:  «April showers» means what? | *A short period of rain or snow | Sparks from a fire | A lot of gifts | A party for a baby
exam:  «Stinging eyes come from chloramines, so shower before you swim.» Which meaning fits best? | *To wash under a shower | A party where people bring presents | A short burst of rain | A shower of sparks
